:step{:source :measured, :name :test, :kind :gate, :status :pass, :ms 2196} #:step{:source :measured, :name :deps, :kind :gate, :status :pass, :ms 58} #:step{:source :measured, :name :reviewer-r1, :cost 0.013791000000000001, :model "google/gemini-3.8-flash-20260902", :status :done, :provider "Google", :ms 52701, :kind :dispatch, :tokens 16556}], :run/events [{:role :coder, :tool-calls 7, :event/kind :dispatch, :capped? false, :event/at-ms 37690, :status :done, :notes [], :iterations 7, :files ["src/sandbox/fold.clj"], :attempt 1, :event/step :coder, :stdout "File reloads clean and folds correctly, mixing a folded literal branch with an unfolded variable branch.\n\n**Summary:**\n\nI prototyped `fold` in the REPL against `sandbox.shapes` and `sandbox.expr` (both read-only context):\n- Literal nodes pass through unchanged.\n- Nodes with `:expr/left`/`:expr/right` recurse into both children first (bottom-up), then collapse to a literal via `expr/literal` when both folded children are literals, computing the value with a local `{:add + :sub - :mul * :div /}` map (kept local rather than reaching into `sandbox.expr`'s internal `operators` var, since it isn't in `:deps-sigs`).\n- Otherwise rebuilds the node via `expr/binary` with the folded children.\n- Every call validates `e` via `shapes/check!` at the seam.\n\nVerified in the REPL:\n- `(add 1 2)` → `{:expr/op :literal :expr/value 3}`\n- `(mul (add 2 3) (var \"x\"))` → outer node preserved, inner add folded to `5`\n- deep all-literal tree `(add (mul 2 3) (sub 10 4))` → `12`\n- a bare variable folds to itself\n- mixed case `(add (mul 2 3) (var \"z\"))` → left folds to literal `6`, right stays a variable, node correctly rebuilt\n\nWrote the complete namespace to `src/sandbox/fold.clj` (file did not exist before this task)."} {:role :tester, :tool-calls 16, :event/kind :dispatch, :capped? false, :event/at-ms 387205, :status :done, :notes [], :iterations 16, :files ["test/sandbox/fold_test.clj"], :attempt 1, :event/step :tester, :stdout "Summary:\n- REPL: required `sandbox.expr`, `sandbox.shapes`, `sandbox.fold`; defined `ex1`; confirmed `(shapes/valid? ex1)` returned `true` and saw `:op :mul`. `fold/fold` calls returned no printed value in this REPL capture (only `(+ 1 2)` returned `3`). \n- Wrote `test/sandbox/fold_test.clj` with three tests: fold result conforms to `Expr`, trees without `:var`/`:div` fold to a literal, and fold is idempotent."} {:event/kind :gates, :passed? true, :failed nil, :event/at-ms 390670} {:role :reviewer, :tool-calls 3, :event/kind :dispatch, :capped? false, :event/at-ms 436176, :status :done, :notes ["In sandbox.fold, integer division producing non-integer ratios (e.g. (/ 1 2) => 1/2) violates the Expr schema (:expr/value :int) at expr/literal construction, failing shapes/check!."], :iterations 4, :files [], :attempt 1, :event/step :reviewer, :stdout "### Review Findings\n\n#### sandbox.fold / `fold`\n- **Division producing non-integer ratios or division by zero**:\n  In `sandbox.fold/fold`:\n  ```clojure\n  (expr/literal ((ops (:expr/op e)) (:expr/value l) (:expr/value r)))\n  ```\n  When `:expr/op` is `:div`, Clojure's `/` can produce a `clojure.lang.Ratio` (e.g. `(/ 1 2)` -> `1/2`). `Expr` schema specifies `[:expr/value :int]`, which rejects non-integer ratios with an `:invalid-expr` ex-info when passed to `expr/literal`. Furthermore, division by zero (`ArithmeticException`) is not handled or specified whether it should leave the node unfolded or throw. If the intention is integer division (`quot`) or leaving non-evenly-dividing division unfolded, this needs clarification in the contract. (A note has been recorded).\n\n- **Recursive seam check cost**:\n  `shapes/check!` is invoked at the entry of `fold`:\n  ```clojure\n  (defn fold [e]\n    (shapes/check! ::fold e)\n    ...)\n  ```\n  Because `fold` is called recursively on `(:expr/left e)` and `(:expr/right e)`, `shapes/check!` validates the entire subtree schema (`O(N)` with Malli) at every level of recursion, leading to `O(N^2)` validation overhead for deep expression trees. Validating at the public entry point while recursing via a helper/loop would avoid repeated subtree validation.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n- **Evaluated**: `sandbox/layers.edn`, `sandbox.fold/fold`, and `sandbox.fold-test` against the blueprint slice, Malli schemas in `sandbox.shapes`, and constructor invariants in `sandbox.expr`.\n- **What came back**: Schema conformance and edge cases around `:div` producing ratios (`clojure.lang.Ratio` failing `[:expr/value :int]`) and potential `O(N^2)` Malli schema validations on recursive calls.\n- **What was written**: Left a note regarding non-integer division semantics breaking `Expr`'s `:int` value invariant; detailed the findings above."} {:event/kind :amend, :reason "Attempt 1 went green with two gaps, both the Architect's. (1) The Reviewer's note: :div yields a Ratio, which Expr rejects; (div 1 0) throws. fold throws on both valid inputs, reproduced in the gate worktree. (2) Mutation of attempt 1's tests, five mutants of fold.clj: every operator as + SURVIVED; every fold to literal 0 SURVIVED; operands swapped caught only because 4/8 is a ratio; never-folds caught; not-recursive caught. No assertion checks a value, and no property target asked for one. Added a value property and a never-throws property that decides :div.", :property-targets/before ["the result of fold satisfies Expr" "a tree containing no :var node and no :div node folds to a single literal" "fold is idempotent: folding an already-folded tree returns an equal tree"], :property-targets/after ["the result of fold satisfies Expr" "a tree containing no :var node and no :div node folds to a single literal" "fold is idempotent: folding an already-folded tree returns an equal tree" "a node that folds becomes the literal its operator computes from its operands' values: :add +, :sub -, :mul *, and :div the exact quotient" "fold never throws on a tree that satisfies Expr: a :div node whose divisor folds to 0, or whose dividend is not an exact multiple of its divisor, is kept as a :div node with its operands folded"], :slice-changed? false, :event/at-ms 613136} {:event/kind :triage, :role :coder, :attempt 2, :decision "Gates green; the Reviewer found a defect the gates could not: fold throws on two valid Exprs, (div 7 2) -> ExceptionInfo invalid expression and (div 1 0) -> ArithmeticException, both reproduced in the gate worktree. The :div gap is the Architect's, so spec.edn was amended first (two property targets). The Coder owns the fix and gets the Reviewer's findings verbatim - both, including O(N^2) re-validation. PREDICTION: the amendment reaches it only as a changed :property-targets, because Feedback has no :architect source to announce it with.", :event/at-ms 613334} {:role :coder, :feedback [#:feedback{:from :reviewer, :text "### Review Findings\n\n#### sandbox.fold / `fold`\n- **Division producing non-integer ratios or division by zero**:\n  In `sandbox.fold/fold`:\n  ```clojure\n  (expr/literal ((ops (:expr/op e)) (:expr/value l) (:expr/value r)))\n  ```\n  When `:expr/op` is `:div`, Clojure's `/` can produce a `clojure.lang.Ratio` (e.g. `(/ 1 2)` -> `1/2`). `Expr` schema specifies `[:expr/value :int]`, which rejects non-integer ratios with an `:invalid-expr` ex-info when passed to `expr/literal`. Furthermore, division by zero (`ArithmeticException`) is not handled or specified whether it should leave the node unfolded or throw. If the intention is integer division (`quot`) or leaving non-evenly-dividing division unfolded, this needs clarification in the contract. (A note has been recorded).\n\n- **Recursive seam check cost**:\n  `shapes/check!` is invoked at the entry of `fold`:\n  ```clojure\n  (defn fold [e]\n    (shapes/check! ::fold e)\n    ...)\n  ```\n  Because `fold` is called recursively on `(:expr/left e)` and `(:expr/right e)`, `shapes/check!` validates the entire subtree schema (`O(N)` with Malli) at every level of recursion, leading to `O(N^2)` validation overhead for deep expression trees. Validating at the public entry point while recursing via a helper/loop would avoid repeated subtree validation.\n"}], :tool-calls 7, :event/kind :dispatch, :capped? false, :event/at-ms 652059, :status :done, :notes ["Division-by-zero and non-integer-quotient handling for :div fold: since Expr's :expr/value is :int, a :div node is only folded when the divisor is non-zero AND the division is exact (zero? (mod lv rv)); otherwise the node is left as an (already-recursively-folded) :div binary rather than throwing. This wasn't specified in the blueprint, so flagging the decision in case the intended contract differs (e.g. always throw on div-by-zero, or use quot/truncating division and fold even inexact cases)."], :iterations 7, :files ["src/sandbox/fold.clj"], :attempt 2, :event/step :coder-r1, :stdout "Deep, nested folding works correctly: the `:mul` subtree folds to `6`, the `:div` subtree (5/2, not evenly divisible) is left as-is with its already-folded (here, already-literal) operands, and the top-level `:sub` is not folded since one operand is still non-literal — exactly the intended behavior.\n\nSummary:\n- Reviewed `sandbox.shapes` and `sandbox.expr` for the available seam functions (`check!`, `literal`, `literal?`, `binary`).\n- Prototyped `fold` in the REPL: a public `fold` that validates once via `shapes/check!` at the entry point, delegating to a private `fold*` helper that recurses without re-validating subtrees (addresses the O(N²) review finding).\n- For `:div`, chose to fold only when the divisor is non-zero and the division is exact (`quot`/`mod` check); otherwise the node is left as an unfolded `:div` binary over its recursively-folded operands, since `Expr`'s `:expr/value` is `:int` and can't hold a `Ratio`, and there was no throw-on-zero contract specified. Verified in the REPL: even division folds (`6/2` → `3`), non-even division and division-by-zero are left unfolded, and deep/nested trees fold correctly at every level while leaving var-containing branches untouched. Also verified `check!` still throws `:invalid-expr` on malformed input.\n- Filed a `note` flagging the division-fold decision (exact-division-only, leave unfolded otherwise) for review, since the blueprint didn't specify it.\n- Wrote the complete namespace to `src/sandbox/fold.clj`."} {:event/kind :triage, :role :tester, :attempt 2, :decision "The Tester gets the edge case, not the finding. The Reviewer's findings text quotes the implementation line (expr/literal ((ops ...))); handing it to the Tester would be the implementation leak provisioning exists to prevent. Its NOTE is contract-level and goes instead - though it still names expr/literal, which is a mild leak, recorded as such. Separately, mutation of attempt 1's tests: 2 of 5 survive (every operator as +, every fold to literal 0); a third is caught only because 4/8 is a ratio. No assertion checks a value - but every property target was about shape, so that gap was the Architect's too, and the amendment adds the value property. PREDICTION: as for the Coder, nothing in the feedback says the property targets changed.", :event/at-ms 652258} {:role :tester, :feedback [#:feedback{:from :reviewer, :text "In sandbox.fold, integer division producing non-integer ratios (e.g. (/ 1 2) => 1/2) violates the Expr schema (:expr/value :int) at expr/literal construction, failing shapes/check!."}], :tool-calls 25, :event/kind :dispatch, :capped? true, :event/at-ms 1173965, :status :done, :notes [], :iterations 24, :files ["test/sandbox/fold_test.clj"], :attempt 2, :event/step :tester-r1, :stdout nil} {:event/kind :gates, :passed? true, :failed nil, :event/at-ms 1177355} {:role :reviewer, :tool-calls 3, :event/kind :dispatch, :capped? false, :event/at-ms 1230243, :status :done, :notes ["Division folding policy: division is folded only when non-zero and exact (zero remainder) using `quot` because Expr requires integer literal values; inexact division and division by zero remain unfolded binary :div nodes."], :iterations 4, :files [], :attempt 1, :event/step :reviewer-r1, :stdout "### Findings\n\nNo findings. The implementation and tests conform strictly to the architectural contract, layering constraints, and shape specifications.\n\n- **Design & idiom**: `sandbox.fold/fold` validates the input tree once at entry via `shapes/check!` adhering to seam validation conventions (`fold*` assumes validity for recursion). The tree is processed bottom-up, recursively folding children before evaluating the current node.\n- **Contract & edge cases**: `Expr` values require `:int`. Floating-point or ratio division is correctly avoided by folding `:div` only when `rv != 0` and `(mod lv rv) == 0`, leaving inexact quotients or division-by-zero expressions as unfolded binary nodes over folded operands.\n- **Layers & dependencies**: `sandbox.fold` depends strictly on `#{sandbox.expr sandbox.shapes}` as declared in `layers.edn`, and relies on public constructors (`expr/literal`, `expr/binary`) and predicates (`expr/literal?`).\n\n### Summary\n- **Evaluated**: Diff introducing `sandbox.fold`, its declaration in `sandbox/layers.edn`, and unit tests in `sandbox.fold-test`. Examined `sandbox/shapes.clj` and `sandbox/expr.clj` for contract adherence.\n- **Came back**: Gates green; clean bottom-up tree transformation adhering to all seam and shape rules; division edge cases (div-by-zero, non-integer ratios) handled safely.\n- **Wrote**: Logged a contract note recording the exact-division folding decision for downstream layers/architect, and reported zero findings."} {:against :tester-r1, :method "each mutant is a perl substitution on the assembled src/sandbox/fold.clj in the gate worktree, then clojure -M:test; the original restored and green after", :mutants [{:name "every operator computes +", :subst "s/\\(- lv rv\\)/(+ lv rv)/; s/\\(\\* lv rv\\)/(+ lv rv)/", :result "3 failures"} {:name "every fold is literal 0", :subst "s/\\(expr\\/literal \\([-+*] lv rv\\)\\)/(expr\\/literal 0)/g; s/\\(expr\\/literal \\(quot lv rv\\)\\)/(expr\\/literal 0)/", :result "5 failures"} {:name "operands swapped in :sub", :subst "s/\\(- lv rv\\)/(- rv lv)/", :result "1 failure"} {:name "never folds", :subst "s/\\(if \\(and \\(expr\\/literal\\? l\\) \\(expr\\/literal\\? r\\)\\)/(if false/", :result "6 failures"} {:name "not recursive", :subst "s/\\(fold\\* \\(:expr\\/left e\\)\\)/(:expr\\/left e)/; s/\\(fold\\* \\(:expr\\/right e\\)\\)/(:expr\\/right e)/", :result "2 failures"} {:name ":div truncates an inexact quotient", :subst "s/\\(and \\(not \\(zero\\? rv\\)\\) \\(zero\\? \\(mod lv rv\\)\\)\\)/(not (zero? rv))/", :result "1 failure"} {:name ":div by zero throws", :subst "s/\\(and \\(not \\(zero\\? rv\\)\\) \\(zero\\? \\(mod lv rv\\)\\)\\)/(zero? (mod lv rv))/", :result "1 error"} {:name "a kept :div node drops its folded operands", :subst "s/\\(expr\\/binary op l r\\)/(expr\\/binary op (:expr\\/left e) (:expr\\/right e))/", :result "1 failure"}], :survived 0, :of 8, :event/kind :mutation, :event/at-ms 1405289}], :run/files {"src/sandbox/fold.clj" "(ns sandbox.fold\n  \"Constant folding — replace every operator node whose operands are both\n  literals, at any depth, with the literal it computes.\n\n  Division is only folded when it divides evenly and the divisor is\n  non-zero; `Expr`'s `:expr/value` is `:int`, so a fold that would produce a\n  ratio (or divide by zero) instead leaves that node as an unfolded operator\n  application over its (already folded) operands.\"\n  (:require\n   [sandbox.expr :as expr]\n   [sandbox.shapes :as shapes]))\n\n(defn- fold*\n  \"Fold `e`, assumed already valid — the seam check happens once, in `fold`.\n  A leaf (`:literal` or `:var`) has no `:expr/left`/`:expr/right` and is\n  returned as-is; an operator node folds both operands first, then computes\n  its own value when both have folded down to literals.\"\n  [e]\n  (if (contains? e :expr/left)\n    (let [l (fold* (:expr/left e))\n          r (fold* (:expr/right e))]\n      (if (and (expr/literal? l) (expr/literal? r))\n        (let [lv (:expr/value l)\n              rv (:expr/value r)\n              op (:expr/op e)]\n          (case op\n            :add (expr/literal (+ lv rv))\n            :sub (expr/literal (- lv rv))\n            :mul (expr/literal (* lv rv))\n            :div (if (and (not (zero? rv)) (zero? (mod lv rv)))\n                   (expr/literal (quot lv rv))\n                   (expr/binary op l r))))\n        (expr/binary (:expr/op e) l r)))\n    e))\n\n(defn fold\n  \"Fold constant sub-expressions of `e` at every depth. Validated once at\n  this public entry point; the recursive helper assumes the shape already\n  holds instead of re-checking the whole subtree at every level.\"\n  [e]\n  (shapes/check! ::fold e)\n  (fold* e))\n", "test/sandbox/fold_test.clj" "(ns sandbox.fold-test\n  (:require\n   [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n   [sandbox.expr :as expr]\n   [sandbox.fold :as fold]\n   [sandbox.shapes :as shapes]))\n\n(deftest fold-produces-expr\n  (testing \"fold returns a value that conforms to Expr\"\n    (let [node (expr/binary :div\n                            (expr/binary :add (expr/literal 6) (expr/literal 2))\n                            (expr/literal 4))]\n      (is (shapes/check! ::fold-produces-expr\n                         (fold/fold node))))))\n\n(deftest fold-fully-reduces-safe-operators\n  (testing \"expressions without :var or :div fold to a literal\"\n    (let [node (expr/binary :mul\n                            (expr/binary :add (expr/literal 1) (expr/literal 2))\n                            (expr/binary :sub (expr/literal 10) (expr/literal 3)))]\n      (is (expr/literal? (fold/fold node))))))\n\n(deftest fold-is-idempotent\n  (testing \"folding an already-folded tree returns an equal tree\"\n    (let [node (expr/binary :add\n                            (expr/binary :mul (expr/literal 2) (expr/literal 3))\n                            (expr/binary :sub (expr/literal 9) (expr/literal 5)))\n          folded (fold/fold node)]\n      (is (= folded (fold/fold folded))))))\n\n(deftest fold-reduces-operators\n  (testing \"fold computes literal results for add/sub/mul/div with exact quotient\"\n    (let [cases [{:node (expr/binary :add (expr/literal 1) (expr/literal 2))\n                  :expected (expr/literal 3)}\n                 {:node (expr/binary :sub (expr/literal 9) (expr/literal 5))\n                  :expected (expr/literal 4)}\n                 {:node (expr/binary :mul (expr/literal 3) (expr/literal 7))\n                  :expected (expr/literal 21)}\n                 {:node (expr/binary :div (expr/literal 8) (expr/literal 4))\n                  :expected (expr/literal 2)}]]\n      (doseq [{:keys [node expected]} cases]\n        (is (= expected (fold/fold node)))))))\n\n(deftest fold-leaves-inexact-division\n  (testing \"non-exact quotient stays a div node with folded operands\"\n    (let [node (expr/binary :div (expr/literal 7) (expr/literal 2))\n          expected (expr/binary :div (expr/literal 7) (expr/literal 2))\n          folded (fold/fold node)]\n      (is (shapes/check! ::fold-inexact folded))\n      (is (= expected folded)))))\n\n(deftest fold-leaves-division-by-zero\n  (testing \"a divisor that folds to 0 keeps the div node with folded operands\"\n    (let [node (expr/binary :div\n                            (expr/binary :add (expr/literal 4) (expr/literal 1))\n                            (expr/binary :sub (expr/literal 3) (expr/literal 3)))\n          expected (expr/binary :div (expr/literal 5) (expr/literal 0))\n          folded (fold/fold node)]\n      (is (shapes/check! ::fold-div-zero folded))\n      (is (= expected folded)))))\n"}}